An architectural breakdown, execution flow review, and evaluation of **Sample 10: Walk-Forward Validated MA-Crossover Tranche Engine**.

---

## 🛠️ What Does This Script Do? (High-Level Summary)

This script is an **Anchored Expanding Walk-Forward Backtesting Engine** designed for Indian Equities (Nifty Universe) using a fixed-tranche capital deployment model.

Instead of running a single Monte Carlo optimization over the entire dataset (which causes lookahead bias and overfitting), it splits historical data into **sequential rolling folds**:

1. **Fold 1:** Train on Years $1 \dots Y$ (e.g., 2015–2019) $\rightarrow$ Freeze parameters $\rightarrow$ Forward-test on Year $Y+1$ (2020) **completely untouched**.
2. **Fold 2:** Train on Years $1 \dots Y+1$ (2015–2020) $\rightarrow$ Freeze parameters $\rightarrow$ Forward-test on Year $Y+2$ (2021).
3. **Fold $N$:** Repeat expanding window through the present year (2026).

It evaluates parameter stability across folds (checking if the selected moving averages drift wildly or stay consistent) and provides a clean, un-peeked Out-of-Sample (OOS) performance record.

---

## 🧭 Complete Path of Decision and Action

```
[1. DATA INGESTION & MATRIX PREPARATION]
       │
       ▼
   • Download 2015–Present daily Open/Close for Nifty Universe + ^NSEI Index via yfinance
   • Mask High-Dividend Stocks (ITC, Coal India, etc.) for bifurcated exit handling
   • Calculate contiguous 2D Open, Close, Index, Year, and Month matrices
       │
       ▼
[2. ANCHORED EXPANDING WALK-FORWARD DRIVER] (`run_walkforward`)
       │
       ├── Set Test Year = Start Year (2015) + Initial Train Years (5) => 2020
       │
       ├── LOOP: For each Test Year (2020, 2021, 2022, 2023, 2024, 2025, 2026):
       │     │
       │     ├───► A. IN-SAMPLE FIT (`search_best_params` on 2015 -> Test_Year - 1):
       │     │       • Execute 60,000 Monte Carlo Random Draws
       │     │       • Compute Numba Portfolio Engine (`evaluate_portfolio`)
       │     │       • Enforce In-Sample Consistency Gate (Vintage Win Rate >= 55% vs ^NSEI)
       │     │       • Enforce In-Sample Neighbor Perturbation Check (±2 days MA shift >= 80% score)
       │     │       • Select Champion Configuration for this fold
       │     │
       │     └───► B. OUT-OF-SAMPLE TEST:
       │             • Freeze Champion Parameters
       │             • Extend evaluation array through current Test_Year
       │             • Read off ONLY the isolated Test_Year return
       │             • Compare Strategy Return vs ^NSEI Index Return (WIN / LOSS)
       │
       ▼
[3. OOS REPORTING & PARAMETER STABILITY DIAGNOSTIC] (`summarize_folds`)
       │
       ├── Print per-fold OOS Strategy vs. Index comparison table
       ├── Measure Parameter Drift: Calculate Std Dev of Short/Long MAs picked per fold
       └── Output final Out-of-Sample Win Rate & Excess Return Summary

```

---

## 🔍 Detailed Operational & Math Architecture

### 1. Fixed-Tranche Deployment Sizing

* **Fixed Amount:** `TRANCHE_SIZE = 8000.0` (INR).
* **Why Fixed Sizing?** Sizing positions as a percentage of Net Asset Value (NAV) causes late-stage bets in a compounding portfolio to balloon in absolute size. This concentrates the terminal return into a few late trades. Fixed tranches keep trade-level statistical edge unskewed over time.

### 2. Bifurcated Exit Architecture (`evaluate_portfolio`)

Different asset profiles receive custom exit rules inside the Numba kernel:

* **High-Dividend Names (`div_mask == True`):** Routine MA crossunders are ignored to hold for dividend accumulation. Positions liquidate **only** on structural breakdowns (`Close < Super_MA * (1 - struct_dip_pct)`).
* **Growth / Momentum Names (`div_mask == False`):** Evaluated against one of 3 selectable exit families:
* `Exit Mode 0:` Standard MA Crossunder ($MA_{\text{short}} < MA_{\text{long}}$).
* `Exit Mode 1:` Trailing Stop Loss ($Close < Peak \times (1 - tsl\_pct)$) OR Structural Dip.
* `Exit Mode 2:` Crossunder OR Trailing Stop Loss OR Structural Dip.



### 3. In-Sample Consistency Gate & Parameter Drift Check

Before a configuration is chosen for an OOS fold test, it must pass two checks:

* **Vintage Win Rate Gate:** The strategy must beat the benchmark index in at least 55% of the in-sample training years (`WIN_RATE_THRESHOLD = 0.55`).
* **Parameter Stability Diagnostic:** If selected Short/Long MAs jump erratically across folds (e.g., Short MA = 12 in Fold 1, 75 in Fold 2, 22 in Fold 3), the engine warns that the optimizer is fitting random noise in training windows rather than isolating a true structural edge.

